## 6. Design System Terminology Glossary

For AI-parseable design briefs, here are the exact terms to use:

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Hero-Driven Long Scroll` | Full-viewport hero section followed by scrollable content sections |
| `Capsule CTA / Pill Button` | Rounded-full button with uppercase tracking-wide text |
| `Micro-Conversion Widget` | Low-barrier lead capture (1-2 fields) before full form |
| `Trust Bar / Social Proof Strip` | Horizontal row of credibility indicators (badges, counters, press logos) |
| `Progressive Disclosure Form` | Multi-step form that reveals fields progressively to reduce initial cognitive load |
| `Sticky FAB (Floating Action Button)` | Fixed-position action button (usually bottom-right) for instant contact |
| `Lead Gate Modal` | A popup that exchanges value (brochure/guide) for contact information |
| `Scarcity Badge` | Visual indicator showing limited availability ("Only 4 left") |
| `Exit-Intent Overlay` | Modal triggered when cursor moves toward browser close/back |
| `Authority Marker` | Trust symbol showing regulatory compliance, awards, or endorsements |
| `Bento Grid` | Multi-card grid with varying card sizes (inspired by Japanese bento boxes) |
| `Glassmorphism Panel` | Translucent card/panel with backdrop-blur and border-white/10 |
| `Zebra Stripe Sections` | Alternating dark and light section backgrounds for visual rhythm |
| `Lifestyle Card` | Property card that emphasizes aspirational imagery over specifications |
| `Soft-Pill Form` | Input fields with large border-radius (16-24px), icon prefixed |
| `Hotspot Overlay` | Interactive image with clickable points revealing contextual info |
| `Numbered Slide Indicator` | Carousel pagination showing "01", "02", "03" with progress bars |
| `Sticky Sidebar CTA` | Fixed-position sidebar panel that follows scroll on property detail pages |
| `Fixed Bottom Bar` | Mobile-only fixed bar at screen bottom with key actions |

---

## 7. Summary Verdict

### What the Site Does Well ✅
- **Premium visual aesthetic** — The Swiss-Minimal / Editorial Luxury design immediately communicates high-end positioning
- **Clean typography hierarchy** — Effective use of micro-labels, bold headlines, and medium-weight body text
- **Interactive engagement** — Hotspot explorer, carousel, hover effects create a polished experience
- **Responsive design** — Thoughtful mobile breakpoints throughout
- **Property detail page** — Sticky sidebar CTA, gallery, amenities, and advisor contact is a strong layout pattern

### What Needs Fixing 🚨
- **Dead buttons everywhere** — Multiple CTAs lead nowhere (brochure download, schedule visit on detail, explore homes)
- **Trust comes too late** — Testimonials are after the form; no RERA, no press logos, no award badges
- **Form friction too high** — 6-field form for cold traffic on ₹8-48Cr products
- **No instant contact** — No WhatsApp, no live chat, no floating phone — critical in Indian luxury real estate
- **Placeholder/template artifacts** — picsum.photos images, "Powered by Webflow" text, duplicate team members
- **Broken cross-page CTAs** — "Schedule a Visit" only works on homepage

> **Current Estimated Conversion Rate:** 0.5–1.5% (industry average for luxury real estate with friction)
> **Projected After Optimization:** 3–6% (with all P0 + P1 fixes implemented)
